[
    {
        "content": "<p>Is this behavior intended?</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- error, as expected</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span>\n\n<span class=\"c1\">-- no error!?</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599646311,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780444235
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(it looks like it can be fixed by using <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Lean.Elab.Tactic.tryCatch#doc\">docs#Lean.Elab.Tactic.tryCatch</a> instead)</p>",
        "id": 599647588,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780444840
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well, <code>evalTactic</code> ends up throwing an internal <code>throwAbortTerm</code> exception and we revert to before all error messages. I suppose you are expected to \"try something else\" in the <code>catch</code> block and basically ignore the error. For example, I claim this works as intended:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Just prints \"All fine\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"All fine\"</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>So with all the error messages reverted, <code>throw x</code> has not much chance of doing anything useful.</p>",
        "id": 599711865,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780471372
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873547\">Robin Arnez</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/try.20_.20catch.20x.20.3D.3E.20throw.20x.20is.20not.20a.20no-op.3F/near/599711865\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Well, <code>evalTactic</code> ends up throwing an internal <code>throwAbortTerm</code> exception and we revert to before all error messages</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>The fact that the <code>try</code> does this reverting is surprising to me</p>",
        "id": 599712882,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780471663
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Though I guess I am also surprised by <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/try.20catch.20and.20mut/near/599715095\">#lean4 &gt; try catch and mut @ 💬</a> so maybe my intuition for <code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> from other languages is misguided</p>",
        "id": 599713338,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780471797
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Well I think the canonical use of tactic <code>try catch</code> is how it's used in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/1c71c358391e3b823dcf0edce5b3c65ed6c37351/src/Lean/Elab/Tactic/BuiltinTactic.lean#L242-L247\"><code>any_goals</code></a>:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mvarIdsNew</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mvarIdsNew</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">++</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">getUnsolvedGoals</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">succeeded</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span>\n<span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">mvarIdsNew</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mvarIdsNew</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">push</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mvarId</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>In this case, we don't wanna keep around all the error messages from failed tactics.</p>",
        "id": 599714145,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780472006
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/try.20_.20catch.20x.20.3D.3E.20throw.20x.20is.20not.20a.20no-op.3F/near/599713338\">schrieb</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Though I guess I am also surprised by<br>\n...<br>\nso maybe my intuition for <code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> from other languages is misguided</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>You're right, this is confusing; but well, local imperativity has its limits and this turns out to be one of them.</p>",
        "id": 599714672,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780472156
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Maybe we should get a warning here if you assign a mutable variable inside of a try and also use it later?</p>",
        "id": 599714998,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Arnez",
        "timestamp": 1780472237
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think perhaps what I'd argue for here is that \"try and revert\" and \"try and resume\" are both useful operators, and it's confusing that which one<code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> syntax is allocated to depends on the monad:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: inside try -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_cmd</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inside try\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"nevermind\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: inside try -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"n\">run_meta</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inside try\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"nevermind\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- info: inside try -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">by_elab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inside try\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"nevermind\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">return</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">const</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`True.intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>yet:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- -/</span>\n<span class=\"bp\">#</span><span class=\"n\">guard_msgs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">True</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"inside try\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"nevermind\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">()</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">trivial</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599715657,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780472422
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Though I guess we're sort of doomed with <code>StateT S (ExceptT E m)</code> vs <code>ExceptT E (StateT S m)</code>, which naturally inherit different behaviors around state reversion, and <code>[MonadExcept E m'] [MonadState S m']</code> can't distinguish between them.</p>",
        "id": 599718744,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780473170
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I would argue the real explanation for your original question is that <code>.internal</code> exceptions don't produce errors in the editor. Consider the following:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Lean</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Elab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Exception</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">TacticM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">try</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">default</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">evalTactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">stx</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">catch</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error: \"hi\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throwError</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"hi\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- info: \"hi\"; the error is silent</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s2\">\"hi\"</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">internal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599973238,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1780540007
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Only because <code>0</code> is <code>interrupt</code>, <code>#eval InternalExceptionId.mk 0 |&gt;.getName</code></p>",
        "id": 599973718,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780540190
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, indeed some of them are visible. Well, whatever the error here is is apparently one of the invisible ones:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">run_tac</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">do</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"k\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">internal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unreachable!</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">logInfo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">←</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">getName</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- abortTermElab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">throw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">internal</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 599974292,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1780540360
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Oh, OK, I now understand what Robin was saying and how this all makes sense</p>",
        "id": 599975760,
        "sender_full_name": "Albert Smith",
        "timestamp": 1780540733
    }
]